{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoEncoder","doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoDecoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-and-decoding","title":"Encoding and decoding"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecSettings","doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecSettings\/Format-swift.enum","doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecSettings\/BitRateMode-swift.enum","doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecError"],"anchor":"Configuration-and-failures","title":"Configuration and failures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoEncoderStatistics"],"anchor":"Measurement","title":"Measurement"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This optional product exposes "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoDecoder"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecSettings"},{"type":"text","text":" without depending on the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HaishinKit"},{"type":"text","text":" target. Applications"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as VQMetrix can call it directly. The existing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VideoCodec"},{"type":"text","text":", codec registration,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MediaMixer, and RTC\/RTMP\/SRT pipelines are unchanged; importing this product does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"add VP8\/VP9 transport support."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Installation","text":"Installation","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This product is available on main, but is not included in the released 2.3.0 package:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HaishinKit\/HaishinKit.swift.git\",","         branch: \"main\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".product(name: \"VPXHaishinKit\", package: \"HaishinKit.swift\")"},{"type":"text","text":" to your target."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"After publication, replace the main branch with a release containing this product."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Standalone-conversion","text":"Standalone conversion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following function needs no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import HaishinKit"},{"type":"text","text":" or shared codec registration:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import CoreMedia","import VPXHaishinKit","","func roundTrip(_ references: [CMSampleBuffer]) throws -> [CMSampleBuffer] {","    let settings = VPXVideoCodecSettings(bitRate: 1_000_000, format: .vp9)","    let encoder = try VPXVideoEncoder(settings: settings)","    let decoder = try VPXVideoDecoder(format: .vp9)","    defer { encoder.invalidate(); decoder.invalidate() }","    var restored: [CMSampleBuffer] = []","    for reference in references {","        for packet in try encoder.encode(reference) {","            restored += try decoder.decode(packet)","        }","    }","    for packet in try encoder.finish() {","        restored += try decoder.decode(packet)","    }","    return restored","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"decode"},{"type":"text","text":" synchronously return owned Core Media samples. Copying encoded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes and decoded pixels before libvpx reuses its buffers makes retained outputs safe."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The classes are deliberately non-Sendable: create and use each instance on one actor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or serial executor. Software compression runs on that caller; use a worker executor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for UI applications. The APIs throw errors directly rather than dropping outputs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through an asynchronous continuation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Settings-and-lifecycle","text":"Settings and lifecycle","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"VP8 and VP9 use 8-bit SDR 4:2:0. The encoder accepts only video-range planar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"I420 ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kCVPixelFormatType_420YpCbCr8Planar"},{"text":"), with dimensions exactly matching","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"videoSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It passes the three planes and their row strides directly to libvpx","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while the input pixel buffer is locked. The caller is responsible for color-space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conversion, range normalization, and resizing before encoding. NV12, RGB, full-range,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10-bit, and mismatched dimensions are rejected rather than converted implicitly.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Encoded width\/height must be positive even integers, within the codec limit, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their product must not exceed 16,777,216 pixels. VP9 high-bit-depth and 4:4:4 are not supported.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"PTS values must be numeric, epoch zero, and strictly increasing after conversion","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to a microsecond timebase. Numeric positive input durations are preserved to that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precision; otherwise the frame-rate hint provides a duration. The hint must be finite","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and between 0.001 and 1,000,000 fps. Keyframe intervals are timestamp-based, between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one microsecond and one hour, so skipped inputs do not extend the keyframe interval.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Compression uses realtime, zero-lookahead operation with no intentional frame drops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or frame reordering. Average and constant bitrate modes are available. Call ","type":"text"},{"code":"update","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to change bitrate and frame-rate hints. Changing codec, dimensions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bitrate mode, or keyframe interval requires a new encoder and is rejected by ","type":"text"},{"code":"update","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"finish","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drains the encoder and rejects further input; repeated calls return no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packets. ","type":"text"},{"code":"invalidate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" releases resources and is safe to call repeatedly. Construct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"new encoder\/decoder instances to restart.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The decoder consumes raw compressed VP8\/VP9 samples with a matching format description,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and returns NV12 frames with the packet PTS\/duration and decoded full\/video range."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The caller must demultiplex a container and supply packet timing; this module does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read\/write MP4, IVF, or WebM files, nor add RTP\/Enhanced RTMP\/TS framing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only decoded pixel range is signaled here; interpreting and attaching container colorimetry remains the caller’s responsibility."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encoding and decoding follow the package’s existing platform minimums; this module"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does not depend on VideoToolbox pixel transfer. The libvpx 1.17.0 artifact supports arm64, including Apple silicon","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"simulators; it does not include Intel slices. Preserve the libvpx LICENSE and PATENTS"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"notices from libvpx-xcframework when distributing an app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Encoder-statistics","text":"Encoder statistics","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoEncoder\/statistics","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" on the encoder’s actor or serial executor,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then send the value snapshot to VQMetrix’s UI, history store, or report:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let snapshot = encoder.statistics","print(snapshot.submittedFrameCount, snapshot.outputPacketCount, snapshot.encodedByteCount)","print(snapshot.lastEncodingDuration, snapshot.averageEncodingDuration,","      snapshot.maximumEncodingDuration, snapshot.totalEncodingDuration)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Durations are monotonic wall-clock seconds inside successful native frame-encode calls,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"including scheduling delays. They exclude caller conversion, input validation, output","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copying, failed encode calls, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"finish()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" flushing. They are not CPU utilization,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thermal state, energy use, or end-to-end latency. Packet\/byte counters include drained","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output. Counters live for the encoder’s lifetime, survive invalidation, and are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reset by settings updates. Snapshots are Codable and Sendable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Verification","text":"Verification","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Run ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift test --filter VPXVideoCodecTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for both codec round trips, owned outputs,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keyframe timing, settings updates, unsupported input\/dimension rejection, malformed packets, and lifecycle checks.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift run --package-path VPXHaishinKit\/Tests\/Consumer Consumer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exercises a separate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftPM consumer importing only the public VPX API, without linking the HaishinKit core.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The published libvpx 1.17.0 artifact includes embedded DWARF debug information in its static libraries. Retain the final app archive and matching app dSYM for symbolication.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"VPXHaishinKit"}],"title":"VPXHaishinKit","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"VPXHaishinKit","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"abstract":[{"text":"Standalone software VP8 and VP9 encoding and decoding for Apple platforms.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit"]}],"references":{"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit","abstract":[{"text":"Standalone software VP8 and VP9 encoding and decoding for Apple platforms.","type":"text"}],"title":"VPXHaishinKit"},"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit/VPXVideoEncoder/statistics":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoEncoder\/statistics","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit\/vpxvideoencoder\/statistics","title":"statistics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Current lifetime statistics. Read on the same actor or serial executor as encode calls."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Copy this Sendable value to forward a snapshot to a UI, history store, or report."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"statistics"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"VPXVideoEncoderStatistics","preciseIdentifier":"s:13VPXHaishinKit25VPXVideoEncoderStatisticsV"}]},"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit/VPXVideoCodecSettings":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VPXVideoCodecSettings"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecSettings","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit\/vpxvideocodecsettings","abstract":[{"text":"Settings for standalone, 8-bit software VP8\/VP9 compression.","type":"text"}],"title":"VPXVideoCodecSettings","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VPXVideoCodecSettings"}]},"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit/VPXVideoEncoder":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VPXVideoEncoder"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A synchronous encoder. Confine the instance and its calls to one actor or serial executor."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit\/vpxvideoencoder","title":"VPXVideoEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VPXVideoEncoder"}]},"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit/VPXVideoCodecSettings/Format-swift.enum":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Format","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecSettings\/Format-swift.enum","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit\/vpxvideocodecsettings\/format-swift.enum","abstract":[{"text":"The compressed bitstream format.","type":"text"}],"title":"VPXVideoCodecSettings.Format","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Format","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit/VPXVideoCodecError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"VPXVideoCodecError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecError","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit\/vpxvideocodecerror","abstract":[{"text":"A standalone codec failure. Unsupported configurations never select another codec.","type":"text"}],"title":"VPXVideoCodecError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VPXVideoCodecError","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit/VPXVideoCodecSettings/BitRateMode-swift.enum":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BitRateMode","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoCodecSettings\/BitRateMode-swift.enum","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit\/vpxvideocodecsettings\/bitratemode-swift.enum","abstract":[{"text":"The libvpx rate-control strategy. Neither mode guarantees an exact bitrate.","type":"text"}],"title":"VPXVideoCodecSettings.BitRateMode","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BitRateMode","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit/VPXVideoDecoder":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VPXVideoDecoder"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoDecoder","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit\/vpxvideodecoder","title":"VPXVideoDecoder","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A synchronous decoder. Returned frames own their pixel storage; calls must be serialized."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VPXVideoDecoder"}]},"doc://VPXHaishinKit/documentation/VPXHaishinKit/VPXVideoEncoderStatistics":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"VPXVideoEncoderStatistics","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/VPXHaishinKit\/documentation\/VPXHaishinKit\/VPXVideoEncoderStatistics","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/vpxhaishinkit\/vpxvideoencoderstatistics","abstract":[{"text":"A value snapshot of one encoder’s lifetime counters, suitable for reports and cross-actor transfer.","type":"text"}],"title":"VPXVideoEncoderStatistics","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"VPXVideoEncoderStatistics","kind":"identifier"}]}}}